.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt KUBE-RESET 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kube-reset
.Nd take Kubernetes off this machine, after a snapshot to come back to
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
asks for the word
.Ql reset ;
anything else, or no terminal, stops it with nothing touched.
Then, in order, it:
.Bl -enum -compact
.It
snapshots every dataset of the root's pool, as
.Ar pool Ns Pa @pre-kube-reset- Ns Ar timestamp ,
and stops with nothing removed if it cannot; on a root that is not ZFS it
warns that there is nothing to come back to;
.It
runs
.Ql kubeadm reset -f ;
.It
removes
.Pa /etc/kubernetes Ns 's
manifests, certificates and configurations,
.Pa /var/lib/kubelet ,
.Pa /var/lib/etcd
and
.Pa /root/.kube/config ;
.It
flushes the iptables rules and the CNI state kube-proxy or Cilium left;
.It
restarts containerd.
.El
.Pp
The packages stay installed.
It runs itself under
.Xr sudo 8 .
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print what it removes and exit 0, without root.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 when done, and when it was not confirmed; 1 when the snapshot could not
be taken.
.Sh EXAMPLES
In a Fedora 44 container, with
.Xr zfs 8
replaced by a script that lists a root pool and refuses the snapshot, and
a file in
.Pa /var/lib/etcd :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# echo reset | kube-reset

WARNING: This will tear down Kubernetes on this node.
  - kubeadm reset (drains and removes node from cluster)
  - Removes /etc/kubernetes, /var/lib/etcd, /var/lib/kubelet state
  - Cilium and all pods will be destroyed

cannot create snapshot: out of space
[kube-reset] could not take rpool@pre-kube-reset-20260930T101341Z; nothing has been removed
# (exited 1)
.Ed
.Pp
The file in
.Pa /var/lib/etcd
was still there.
With no terminal:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# kube-reset </dev/null
Aborted.
# (exited 0)
.Ed
.Pp
Coming back, on a kldload machine; not run for this page:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# rollback to pre-kube-reset-<timestamp>
# zfs rollback <dataset>@pre-kube-reset-<timestamp>
# the second for each dataset that holds etcd, kubelet or containerd state
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr kubeadm 1 ,
.Xr kldload-rollback 8 ,
.Xr kube-cluster 8 ,
.Xr kube-status 8 ,
.Xr zfs-rollback 8
.Sh HISTORY
On 2026-09-30, writing this page, in a container: a snapshot that failed
was reported as taken, and etcd was removed anyway; and the way back it
printed,
.Ql zfs rollback -r Ar pool Ns @ Ns Ar snapshot ,
rolls back only the pool's top dataset, which on kldload holds nothing.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An kldload Aq Mt anthony@kldload.com
.Sh CAVEATS
.Ql iptables -F
flushes every rule in those tables, the host's own among them.
